Z||000020||88formula||11-05-1999||09:33 PM|||| 84 Fiero Super Duty Four 6.3 seconds, 85 Fiero SE 6.9 seconds, 88 Formula 6.9 seconds, 86 GT 7.5 seconds, 85GT auto 8.5 seconds, all 0-60 times. I found these statistics from this web site. <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/topfiero/per.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/topfiero/per.txt</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||pollock||11-09-1999||10:06 AM||||I've driven 3 86 V6 Fieros, 4spd GT, auto GT, and 4spd SE.  The SE was the quickest, but i think it was because it had 14" wheels, which helped out the gear ratio.  <BR>After that experience, i'll be very conservative on wheel/tire diameter.||||reg||4
Z||000022||stsmithgt||11-10-1999||04:38 PM||||With about 120,000  miles on my 86, it's still damn quick and cruises down the country roads at 115 without a trouble.  Well except for last Sunday I had a shift cable quietly broke.  It definitly slowed my Sunday drive down having only second gear.  I'll replace both of them since it broke where it crosses the exhaust pipe, I imagine the other is ready to go too.||||reg||1
